.TH BOX-MIGRATE 1 "November 2026" "Box-Migrate 0.9.0" "User Commands"

.\" ============================================================================
.SH NAME
.\" ============================================================================

box-migrate \- migrate packages, repositories, and caches between Toolbox containers

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
.I SOURCE DESTINATION
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.\" ============================================================================
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
migrates manually installed packages from an existing Linux Toolbox container
to a newly created destination container.
.PP
The destination is created using the specified distribution and release.
Box-Migrate identifies the source package manager, exports its manually
installed package list, compares it against packages already installed in
the destination, and installs packages not already present.
.PP
Repository configuration, GPG keys, and local package caches can also be
transferred. Repository and cache migration are enabled by default and can
be disabled independently.
.PP
By default, the source container is not modified. The destination is created
as a separate container.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH OPTIONS
.\" ============================================================================

.SS Destination

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-distro " " DISTRO
Specify the distribution for the destination container.
This option is required.
.IP
Must be a distribution natively supported by
.BR toolbox\-create (1):
.BR fedora ,
.BR rhel ,
.BR ubuntu ,
or
.BR arch .

.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-release " " RELEASE
Specify the distribution release for the destination container.
This option is required.

.SS Migration

.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Run in dry-run mode. Source package, repository, and cache data are still
exported, but the destination is not created,
.B rpmrebuild
is not run, and packages are not installed.
.IP
Package comparison uses an empty destination package list, so the displayed
package count is not a prediction of the final installation count.

.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-repos
Enable migration of repository configuration and GPG keys.
This is the default.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-repos
Disable repository configuration and GPG key migration.

.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cache
Enable migration of local package caches.
This is the default.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Disable local package cache migration.

.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-rebuild\-local
Rebuild and migrate standalone local RPM packages (installed from
.I @commandline
without an associated repository) using
.BR rpmrebuild (1)
via
.BR sudo (8).
.IP
This option is disabled by default and applies only to DNF-based
distributions. If
.B rpmrebuild
is not already present in the source container, it will be installed there
before rebuilding the packages.

.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workdir " " DIR
Specify the working directory used to store exported package lists,
repository archives, package caches, rebuilt RPMs, and migration reports.
.IP
By default, files are saved to
.IR ~/box-migrate-SOURCE-to-DESTINATION/ ,
appending a numbered suffix
.RI ( \-1 ,
.IR \-2 ,
and so on) if the directory already exists. When
.B \-\-workdir
is specified, the given directory is used directly and created if it does
not exist. Because Toolbox containers mount your home directory, choose a
path inside
.I $HOME
so container commands can write to it.

.SS General

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the usage information and exit.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" ============================================================================

.TP
.B Migrate Fedora 44 to Fedora 45
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45
.fi

.TP
.B Preview a Fedora migration
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45 --dry-run
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate and rebuild standalone local RPMs on Fedora
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45 --rebuild-local
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate RHEL and save logs to a custom directory
.nf
box-migrate rhel-toolbox-9.4 rhel-toolbox-9.5 -d rhel -r 9.5 -w ~/migrations/rhel-9.5
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate Ubuntu without package caches
.nf
box-migrate ubuntu-toolbox-22.04 ubuntu-toolbox-24.04 --distro ubuntu --release 24.04 --no-cache
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate Arch Linux without repositories
.nf
box-migrate arch-toolbox-latest arch-toolbox-2026 -d arch -r latest --no-repos
.fi

.TP
.B Skip both repositories and caches
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45 --no-repos --no-cache
.fi

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SUPPORTED DISTRIBUTIONS
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
supports only the distributions supported out of the box by
.BR toolbox\-create (1).
Custom container images (such as Debian, Rocky Linux, or AlmaLinux) are not
currently supported.

.TP
.B DNF
.B fedora
and
.B rhel
(allowing migrations such as
.B fedora
to
.BR fedora ,
or
.B rhel
to
.BR rhel ).

.TP
.B APT
.B ubuntu

.TP
.B Pacman
.B arch

.PP
Cross-family package migration is not supported. Both containers must use
the same package manager.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH MIGRATION DETAILS
.\" ============================================================================

.SS Packages

The source package list is obtained using the package manager's manually
installed package records. Packages already installed in the destination
(matched by exact package name) are excluded from the installation list.
.PP
Package availability depends on the destination distribution and its
configured repositories. Packages that are unavailable or incompatible are
skipped when supported by the package manager and logged in the migration
reports.

.SS Standalone local RPMs

On DNF-based distributions, user-installed packages originating from
.I @commandline
(such as one-off local
.I .rpm
files installed without an accompanying repository) are detected and listed
in
.IR special\-cases.txt .
.PP
By default, these packages are not automatically rebuilt, leaving the source
container untouched so you can either download an updated package for the
destination release or reinstall manually.
.PP
When
.B \-\-rebuild\-local
is specified, standalone local packages are excluded from the standard
repository installation pass. Instead,
.B box\-migrate
reconstructs binary
.I .rpm
archives (matched by
.IR name.arch )
from the installed files in the source container via
.B sudo rpmrebuild
(so restricted root-owned files can be read) and installs them into the
destination container. Any packages that fail to rebuild are recorded in
.IR special\-cases.txt .

.SS Repositories and GPG keys

When repository migration is enabled, custom repository configuration and
associated key files are archived from the source and extracted into the
destination (excluding default Fedora and Ubuntu base repository files).
.PP
For DNF-based distributions, release-prefixed source version strings
(such as
.IR fedora-44 ,
.IR fc44 ,
or
.IR el9 )
in repository URL fields
.RI ( baseurl ,
.IR mirrorlist ,
and
.IR metalink )
in imported
.I .repo
files are automatically normalized to
.I $releasever
so they resolve against the destination release.
.PP
For APT-based distributions (Ubuntu), imported third-party repository
definitions in
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/
have occurrences of the source release codename (such as
.IR jammy )
updated to match the destination release codename (such as
.IR noble ).
.PP
However, third-party repository definitions are not guaranteed to support
the destination release. Review imported repository files and their signing
keys before trusting them in the destination container.

.SS Package caches

When cache migration is enabled, locally cached package files are archived
from the source and extracted into the destination when cached package files
are present. Cached files are not guaranteed to be usable by the destination
package manager or compatible with its release.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH FILES
.\" ============================================================================

.TP
.I ~/box-migrate-SOURCE-to-DESTINATION/
Default working directory containing exported package lists, repository
archives, package caches, rebuilt RPMs, and migration reports (unless
overridden with
.BR \-w / \-\-workdir ).
.IP
If the default working directory already exists, a numbered suffix
.RI ( \-1 ,
.IR \-2 ,
etc.) is added.

.PP
Important generated files include:

.TP
.I packages.txt
List of repository packages selected for migration.

.TP
.I report.txt
Package installation output, when an installation is attempted.

.TP
.I special-cases.txt
Summary of detected missing packages, dependency or transaction issues, and
standalone local RPMs (including rebuild successes and failures when
.B \-\-rebuild\-local
is used).

.TP
.I repositories.tar.gz
Exported repository configuration and key archive.

.TP
.I package-cache.tar.gz
Exported local package cache archive.

.TP
.I local-rpms/
Directory containing reconstructed
.I .rpm
files when
.B \-\-rebuild\-local
is used.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
requires:

.IP \(bu 2
Toolbox.

.IP \(bu 2
Podman.

.IP \(bu 2
Bash.

.IP \(bu 2
A working source Toolbox container.

.PP
The source and destination container names must differ, and the destination
container name must not already exist.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH EXIT STATUS
.\" ============================================================================

.TP
.B 0
The script completed successfully (even if individual unavailable packages
were skipped and logged).

.TP
.B Non-zero
An error occurred during argument validation, container inspection, creation,
or another pre-installation operation.
.IP
If a non-zero exit status occurs after the destination container has already
been created,
.B box-migrate
prints the failing line number and exit code along with a
.B toolbox rm -f
cleanup hint. Inspect the migration logs and container state before retrying.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH NOTES
.\" ============================================================================

The source container is retained after migration. Box-Migrate does not
remove or replace it, and does not modify it unless
.B \-\-rebuild\-local
needs to install
.B rpmrebuild
inside the source container.
.PP
The destination may be created successfully even if some packages are
unavailable or incompatible. Review the installation report and
special-cases report after migration.
.PP
Dry-run mode does not create the destination or install packages. It still
creates a working directory and exports data from the source.
.PP
Repository and GPG key archives should be reviewed before being trusted in
the destination.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SEE ALSO
.\" ============================================================================

.BR toolbox (1),
.BR podman (1),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR rpmrebuild (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR apt (8),
.BR pacman (8)